load @term/seed/structure/space/vector
  find vector-space

# A flag: a nested chain of subspaces, each contained in the next, a point in a line in a plane and so on, or for a
# polytope a vertex on an edge on a face on a cell. Flags are the maximal chains a Coxeter group acts on simply
# transitively, and the flags of the 24-cell number its symmetry-group order, 1152. The form carries the vector space
# the flag is built in.
form flag
  link space, like vector-space
